' 4+1 Process view - Caught state kept in sync across screens
' Version 1.0 - 2026-10-19 - reflects the current working tree
' For: developers adding screens that show or change caught state. Documents the decision to make
' Room the single source of truth: no screen pushes updates to another; every ViewModel observes
' Room LiveData and gets the new data after each insert/delete.
' LiveData only runs its query while observed: a tab in the back stack refreshes when it becomes active again.
' The example starts from PokemonDetailScreen; HomeScreen and PokedexScreen use the same path.
@startuml process-caught-state-sync
!include ../style.puml

title Process view - caught state sync
autonumber

box "Main thread"
    participant PokemonDetailScreen
    participant PokemonDetailViewModel
    participant PokemonRepository
    participant HomeViewModel
    participant PokedexViewModel
end box
box "Room executor"
    participant CaughtPokemonDao
end box
database "Local Database" as LocalDb

PokemonDetailScreen -> PokemonDetailViewModel : toggleCaught()
PokemonDetailViewModel -> PokemonRepository : catchPokemon(name, id)
PokemonRepository -> CaughtPokemonDao : insert(entity) (suspend)
CaughtPokemonDao -> LocalDb : INSERT OR IGNORE
LocalDb --> CaughtPokemonDao : table invalidated
CaughtPokemonDao --> PokemonDetailViewModel : isCaught = true (LiveData)
CaughtPokemonDao --> HomeViewModel : getAll() list (LiveData, if observed)
CaughtPokemonDao --> PokedexViewModel : getAll() list (LiveData, if observed)
@enduml
